Subject: [PATCH 27/31] attnk: round 10 E1 arms (SP = G6_ATTN_CTX3_SP, POS =
 G6_ATTN_POSIDX) and attnk_r10a.sh

An E1 arm is checked for determinism (every byte of repeated poisoned calls equal), for what must not change
(the selected set per row, each key's raw score wherever its slot is, the appended KV / index rows, the error
words; SP alone: indices, scores and probabilities byte for byte), and its error against stock is reported
(max abs / rel of both layers' outputs and of the merged context). An E1 arm the dispatch does not take (POS
past the 2048 bucket) must be byte-identical to stock. ATTNK_NANKEY puts a NaN into one index key's scale
(stock drops the key with error 4, POS keeps it). attnk_r10a.sh runs the sweep (T 2K / 8K / 32K x M 1 / 3 / 8,
the 2048 / 2049 boundary, two sessions, ties, underflowing probabilities) against the served flags.
